---
import Docs from "../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Introduction"
  description="Clink connects the CLI agents on your machine to scripts and MCP clients. One Python package installs both entry points."
  toc={[
    ["install", "Install Clink"],
    ["interfaces", "Choose an interface"],
    ["agents", "Supported agents"],
  ]}
>
  <div class="terminal-figure">
    <div class="terminal-top">
      <span class="led" aria-hidden="true"></span> LOCAL EXECUTION
    </div>
    <div
      class="flow-diagram"
      aria-label="A script or MCP client calls Clink, which invokes a local CLI agent"
    >
      <div>
        <b>Script</b>
        <i>or MCP client</i>
      </div>
      <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div class="node">
        <b>clink</b>
      </div>
      <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div>
        <b>CLI agent</b>
        <i>on your machine</i>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h2 id="install">Install Clink</h2>
  <Code label="Terminal" code="uv tool install clink-cli" />
  <p>
    With <a href="/installation/">both commands installed</a>, you can check
    capabilities without signing in to a model or sending a prompt.
  </p>
  <h2 id="interfaces">Choose an interface</h2>
  <div class="guide-cards">
    <a href="/examples/#generate">
      <code>clink</code>
      <strong>
        Call from a script <span>↗</span>
      </strong>
      <p>Submit one JSON request and read one terminal result.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/quick-start/#claude">
      <code>clink-mcp-server</code>
      <strong>
        Connect an MCP client <span>↗</span>
      </strong>
      <p>Expose 18 tools for consultation, local guidance and native tasks.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
  <h2 id="agents">Supported agents</h2>
  <p>
    The verified agent depends on the operation. Codex and Claude Code support
    generation with explicit models. Grok Build supports its native default.
    Antigravity has verified native MCP tasks and unverified generation.{" "}
    <a href="/reference/#admissions">See the full compatibility table.</a>
  </p>
</Docs>
